From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:11:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Tab completions are made and sent on the player's tick
 thread; a person logging in under a bot's name comes first

A tab completion was handled on the event loop, which waited there for the player's tick thread to
make the completions: up to a tick, or for good if that world's thread was stuck. The server has one
event loop, so every player's reads and writes waited with it - 40 completions sent at once held
another connection's ping for 1,962 ms. The completions are now made and sent from that thread,
and nothing waits for them.

A bot's made-up name could be a real player's, and that player could log in while the bot played:
their UUIDs differ, so two players had one name, and when either left, the name went from the name
map with it. The login now asks a bot of that name to leave first and waits for it, as it does for
a player of the same UUID; the name map lets go of a name only for the player who holds it; and a
bot detached from a stuck world leaves the bots' list too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

